✓ ob-eae · DECISION: primary and fallback Qwen3.5 checkpoint   [● P0 · CLOSED]
Assignee: Claude · Type: decision
Created: 2026-08-02 · Started: 2026-08-02 · Updated: 2026-08-02
Close reason: ADR 0003 written. Primary Qwen/Qwen3.5-4B, fallback Qwen/Qwen3.5-0.8B, decided against config.json read directly from HF rather than the survey summary. Confirmed from primary source: 4B is 32 layers = exactly 24 GDN + 8 full attention with an explicit layer_types array, hidden 2560, 262144 native context, 16/32 linear key/value heads, 128/128 head dims, conv kernel 4. Computed the memory decomposition: GDN state 48MB flat at every context length vs KV cache 128MB@4K rising to 8GB@262K, and an all-full-attention counterfactual of ~32.8GB at 262K, so the hybrid saves ~24.8GB (75%) on a 64GB board. Caught and corrected a figure I had been repeating: the 4B has 32 value heads so its per-layer state is 524,288 floats, not the 262,144 from the GDN-2 paper's 1.3B config. One assumption flagged as open: the n_v_heads x d_k x d_v layout still needs confirming from modeling code (ob-37v).

DESCRIPTION

  Pick one primary checkpoint plus a smaller fallback for fast iteration.     
  Optimize the choice for demonstrating the GDN scaling thesis, not for       
  headline model size: a small model that reaches 262K context tells our story
  better than a larger one that cannot. Record as an ADR.                     



